= Notes =

This quest was broken at or around initial live release and remained so for many years. When fixed in October of 2005 it became possible to complete and rewarded small faction hits and a [[Highway Protector's Mask]], a rather nice ALL/ALL face slot item. The quest was later modified for TLP servers to remove the mask and faction hits prior to the release of Luclin.

In EQL it appears the Cargo Clockwork makes it's trip differently than the quest text or other servers might suggest. Should there be no brave adventurers to help with the bandits the Cargo Clockwork will wait about two ticks then begin walking back to Ak'Anon, trailing the murderous rogues behind all the way. The Cargo Clockwork will heal to 100% almost immediately after each blow lands, and in difficulty zero it easily survives it's walk back to it's starting point. The guards along the way will not assist. Just before it reaches it's home the Cargo Clockwork will despawn and respawn at it's start point, and the trio will rush over to continue their attack. At this point the Cargo Clockwork will fight back and also be capable of taking damage, though still will receive no direct assistance from other npcs. In difficulty zero the highwaymen are easily defeated.

It's possible that in higher difficulties the rogues manage to kill their target and return to their spawn points along the road. Some or all of the rogues may be spotted waiting on the road for their prey long after the event has completed. Should all three remain when a new Cargo Clockwork begins their journey the three will remain indifferent as it passes them heading to the windmills and though, upon returning, the Cargo Clockwork will raise the alarm there is no combat, and after a short pause the journey is resumed and the Cargo Clockwork will return unmolested to it's start.

Also notable are the three bandits' drops aside from their heads. Each always has a [[Fine Steel Dagger]] and Hector, Jerald, and Renaldo each also wield a [[Fine Steel Katana]], [[Fine Steel Rapier]], and [[Fine Steel Spear]] respectively. This is an early source for fine steel as these lads are only level 13.

